      "category": "flood_recovery",
      "label": "FloodSmart: After a Flood",
      "url": "https://www.floodsmart.gov/recover",
      "text": "Recover From a Flood\nRecovering after a flood can feel overwhelming. Following simple steps can help you clean up safely, protect your home and start getting life back to normal.\n-\nStart a claim\nImageContact your flood insurance agent as soon as possible. Quickly starting your claim can speed up the recovery process.\n-\nAppeal a claim\nImageIf your claim is denied or you disagree with the amount, you have options. You can appeal the decision with supporting documents.\n-\nDocument flood damage\nImageBegin your recovery by taking photos and videos of all flood damage before cleaning up.\n-\nThe NFIP’s Recovery Checklist\nImageLearn how to quickly and safely recover from a flood.\n-\nRebuild Better\nImageWhen it’s time to rebuild, you may need to meet local requirements that help you reduce future flood damage.\n-\nSuccess Stories\nImageHear real stories about people who rebuilt stronger after a flood—and found hope and resilience along the way.",
      "error": null,
      "char_count": 943
    },
    {
      "category": "dmv_records",
      "label": "DMV: Replace License",
      "url": "https://www.dmv.ca.gov/portal/driver-licenses-identification-cards/replace-your-driver-license-or-identification-dl-id-card/",
      "text": "If your driver’s license (DL) or identification (ID) card has been lost, stolen, or damaged, you may request a replacement.\nHow to request a replacement DL online\n-\nComplete Replacement Driver’s License Application online\nNote ID cards and commercial driver’s licenses (CDL) are not eligible for this application.\nHow to request a replacement CDL or ID in an office\n-\nComplete a new application\nUse our online application to apply for a replacement CDL or ID card.\n-\nVisit a DMV office to complete the process\nYour replacement request isn’t complete until you go to a DMV office. You may either make an appointment, or check the current walk-in wait list time for your local office.\nBe prepared to pay the appropriate replacement licensing fee, have your photograph validated by DMV, and scan your thumbprint (to protect against identity theft).\n-\nReceive your card in the mail\nYou should receive your new card in the mail within three to four weeks. If you have not received your CDL or ID after 60 days, visit Driver’s License & ID Card Status.",
